{#
  Curated SVG line-icon set for the Organic staff-admin UI, drawn from Lucide
  icon paths at a heavier 2.75 default stroke for a rounder, bolder look.

  Icons are drawn on a 24x24 grid and inherit their color from the
  surrounding text via stroke="currentColor" — pass a `text-*` utility class
  to recolor. They are decorative (aria-hidden="true"); when an icon is a
  control's only visible content, give the control a visually hidden text
  child (<span class="sr-only">...</span>), not an aria-label — sonar-html
  reads this macro call as the button's visible text and reports Web:S7927
  against any aria-label on that control. An unknown name renders an empty
  (invisible) <svg> rather than raising an error, so a typo degrades quietly
  instead of breaking the page.

  The macro itself has no domain or application dependencies; the optional
  `class` argument simply forwards any caller-supplied utility classes (e.g. a
  `text-*` color token or a transform) onto the <svg>.

  The path data in the map below is copied from Lucide (https://lucide.dev),
  distributed under the ISC License; the full text, including the additional
  MIT sublicense covering the subset of icons Lucide inherited from Feather,
  is at https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide/blob/main/LICENSE.

